\name{cellucid_camera_path_duration_set}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_duration_set}
\title{Set a camera path transition time}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_duration_set(viewer, seconds, keyframe)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{seconds}{Seconds of the transition to the next keyframe, at least 0.1; null paces it automatically. A number or \code{NULL} (at least 0.1). Required.}
\item{keyframe}{The keyframe the transition starts at; omitted, every keyframe. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Set how long the camera takes from one keyframe to the next, or from every keyframe to its next.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.duration.set} (Camera path). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{camera-path}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_camera_path_duration_set(viewer,
      seconds = 0.1)
